{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.MesonEmSinhClosedForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.MesonEmSinhClosedForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Invertible.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.meson_EM_closed_form_planck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.meson_EM_closed_form_planck","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/meson-em-sinh-closed-form.lean#L84-L94","doc":"Equivalent form: `1 + ℏ_q − ℏ_q²·⅟2 = 1 + (1 − (q⁻¹)²)·⅟2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.meson_EM_closed_form_inverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.meson_EM_closed_form_inverse","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/meson-em-sinh-closed-form.lean#L77-L82","doc":"Equivalent form: `(3q² − 1)·⅟2·(q⁻¹)² = (3 − (q⁻¹)²)·⅟2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.meson_EM_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.meson_EM_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/meson-em-sinh-closed-form.lean#L64-L75","doc":"The sinh-channel EM correction factor in closed form:\n`1 + ℏ_q − ℏ_q²·⅟2 = (3q² − 1)·⅟2·(q⁻¹)²` (i.e. `(3q² − 1)/(2q²)`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:meson-em-sinh-closed-form","label":"prop:meson-em-sinh-closed-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/meson-em-sinh-closed-form.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ_eq","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/meson-em-sinh-closed-form.lean#L57-L62","doc":"`ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹` — the division-free normal form of the Planck quantum,\nthe identity `(q − 1)·q⁻¹ = 1 − q⁻¹` that the unit relation `q·q⁻¹ = 1`\nsupplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/meson-em-sinh-closed-form.lean#L50-L54","doc":"The substrate Planck quantum `ℏ_q = (q − 1)·q⁻¹ = 1 − q⁻¹`.\n\n`q` is carried as a unit of `R`, so `q⁻¹` is the unit inverse (§7c) and no\nfield structure is required. ","signatureChunk":0}]}